# Execute one planar movement relative to the robot pose at goal execution.
# Goal parameters:
# - `command.position.x`: forward-positive translation from the current position [m].
# - `command.position.y`: left-positive translation from the current position [m].
# - `command.position.deg`: counter-clockwise-positive heading change [deg].
# - `command.speed.acc`: acceleration time [ms]. Default: 1000.
# - `command.speed.dec`: deceleration time [ms]. Default: 1000.
# - `command.speed.xy`: maximum translational speed [m/s]. Default: 0.6; must be positive when x or y is non-zero.
# - `command.speed.w`: maximum angular speed [rad/s]. Default: 0.6; must be positive when deg is non-zero.
# The bridge publishes this command to `/drive/run_pos` and waits for `/drive/run_pos/result`.
TriorbRunPos3 command
---
# True only when the relative movement finishes with status `done`.
bool success
# Terminal value received from `/drive/run_pos/result`: `done`, `failed`, or `stopped`.
string status
# Human-readable terminal details supplied by the Action bridge.
string message
---
# Action bridge lifecycle state, such as `command_sent` or `running`.
# This is not a measured robot pose or movement progress value.
string state
# Human-readable lifecycle details supplied by the Action bridge.
string message
